   "html_text": "Among philosophers, Montessori has been largely neglected, though there are some signs of new interest in applying her work to ongoing philosophical problems not only in the philosophy of education but also, as this entry has shown, to a wide range of philosophical issues. Andrew Colgan’s work (2016) shows the relevance of her epistemology for her philosophy of education. Patrick Frierson has shown how she speaks to current issues in virtue epistemology (2018; 2020), moral philosophy (2021b; 202",
